y 12th century. His contributions laid foundational elements for ecclesiastical governance and spiritual communities that influenced the region for decades.", "significanceCategory": "regional"}, "_editLog": [{"timestamp": "2026-09-16T17:16:30Z", "editorId": "gemini-2.5-flash·cloud·GH#35126760497", "field": "summary", "oldValue": "Alexander of Jülich was a religious figures in Duchy of Jülich (1100, Duchy of Jülich – 1135-07-13), recognized as a landmark figure in the Medieval era. Shaped religious practice and spiritual communities.", "newValue": "Alexander of Jülich, born around 1100 within the nascent Duchy of Jülich and dying on July 13, 1135, emerged as a pivotal ecclesiastical figure in the Lower Rhenish region during the early 12th century. Operating within the complex tapestry of the Holy Roman Empire, his influence was primarily concentrated in the territories governed by the Counts of Jülich. He is recognized for his significant contributions to the development of monastic life and the codification of spiritual practices, laying foundational elements for religious governance that would endure in the region for decades.

